@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# smallpt · The Light Lab
+
+Kevin Beason's [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The page renders automatically, lets you randomize the two sphere colors, choose quality and resolution, reset the scene, and download a completed render as PNG.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+npm start
+```
+
+Open the displayed local HTTP URL (port 11222 by default). The compiled `.wasm` and ES module are included, so running the app does not require a compiler. Serve the repository root; `index.html` references the `public/` directory. Do not open it with `file://`.
+
+## Rebuild
+
+Install Emscripten and make `em++` available on your PATH, then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+npm test
+npm run preview:render
+```
+
+The build emits `public/smallpt.mjs` and `public/smallpt.wasm`. The preview command produces `public/preview.png` using the same WebAssembly renderer, at 256 samples per pixel. It is a loading preview; the browser immediately starts a new live render with the selected 64-sample settings.
+
+Rendering runs in a module Web Worker and sends completed scanlines to a canvas. Starting another render terminates the old worker. No SharedArrayBuffer, cross-origin isolation, backend, image generation service, or graphics library is needed. Google Fonts are optional; local fallback fonts work offline.
+
+The Node smoke test executes the actual browser ES module in an isolated worker-like VM with WebAssembly assertions enabled. It checks incremental rendering, visible opaque output, deterministic seeds, changed seeds, changed sphere colors, and invalid input handling. Node's VM module support currently requires the experimental flag provided by the scripts. With the app running, `npm run test:worker` also tests HTTP module loading, streaming Wasm compilation, and completed pixel transfer through the actual worker code. No browser verification was performed.
+
+## Source and license
+
+`src/smallpt-original.cpp` is the unchanged upstream C++ source. `src/smallpt.cpp` preserves its ray intersection and recursive radiance implementation, replaces the command-line renderer with exported scanline functions, removes OpenMP, and exposes sphere colors and the random seed. The preview palette is a warm reflector and a pale green refractor; the classic Cornell-box walls, geometry, lighting, mirror, and glass materials remain intact.
+
+smallpt is © 2006–2008 Kevin Beason, MIT licensed. See `src/LICENSE.smallpt.txt`.
